<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">25 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 25 September, from 1066 to 1962.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/harold-godwinson" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harold-godwinson.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1066">1066 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">960 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Harold II defeats Harald Hardrada at Stamford Bridge</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King Harold of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> surprised and destroyed the Norwegian army near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a>, killing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-hardrada">Harald Hardrada</a> and Tostig. Three days later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-conqueror">William of Normandy</a> landed in the south, forcing Harold to march back.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1237">1237 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">789 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry III and Alexander II agree the Treaty of York</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-of-england">Henry III of England</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-ii-of-russia">Alexander II</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> agreed that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northumberland">Northumberland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cumberland">Cumberland</a> and Westmorland were subject to English <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>. The treaty fixed the Anglo-Scottish border almost as it remains, ending Scottish attempts to extend the frontier south.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-of-england">Henry III of England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1396">1396 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">630 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bayezid I routs Sigismund's crusaders at Nicopolis</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>, the Ottoman sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayezid-i">Bayezid I</a> routed a crusading army led by King Sigismund of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>. The defeat ended the last large-scale joint <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and left the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> firmly in control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-nicopolis">Battle of Nicopolis</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayezid-i">Bayezid I</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-holy-roman-emperor">Sigismund, Holy Roman Emperor</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1513">1513 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">513 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Balboa becomes the first European to see the Pacific from the Americas</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasco-nunez-de-balboa">Vasco Núñez de Balboa</a> climbed a peak on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isthmus-of-panama">Isthmus of Panama</a> and sighted the 'South Sea'. Days later he waded into the water and claimed it and all its shores for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1555">1555 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">471 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Peace of Augsburg is signed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Agreed between Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a>'s government and the Lutheran princes, the treaty let each ruler in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> choose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutheranism">Lutheranism</a> or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a> as his state's official confession. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calvinism">Calvinism</a> was not allowed until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-westphalia">Peace of Westphalia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-augsburg">Peace of Augsburg</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1643">1643 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">383 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The English Parliament accepts the Solemn League and Covenant</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The English Parliament and the Westminster Assembly accepted the Solemn League and Covenant with the Scottish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/covenanters">Covenanters</a>, already approved by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-scotland">Church of Scotland</a>. It promised religious reforms in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and Ireland in exchange for Scottish troops against King Charles I.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-english-civil-war">First English Civil War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-england">Charles I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1775">1775 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">251 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ethan Allen fails to capture Montreal at Longue-Pointe</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethan-allen">Ethan Allen</a> and a small force of American and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a> militia failed in an attempt to capture <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montreal">Montreal</a> from the British. Major John Brown, who Allen claimed was to bring reinforcements, did not appear, leaving them isolated across the St Lawrence.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethan-allen">Ethan Allen</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montreal">Montreal</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1789">1789 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">237 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress proposes the amendments that become the Bill of Rights</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The First Congress sent twelve proposed amendments to the states. Ten were ratified in 1791 as the Bill of Rights, protecting freedoms of speech, religion, press and assembly.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1962">1962 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">64 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sonny Liston knocks out Floyd Patterson to win the world title</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Sonny Liston took the world heavyweight title in Chicago by knocking out Floyd Patterson in 2 minutes 6 seconds of the first round. He lost the title to Cassius Clay in 1964.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 25 September <span class="n">14</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ashikaga-yoshimitsu"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ashikaga-yoshimitsu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ashikaga Yoshimitsu</span><span class="tp">1358–1408</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gunther-xli-of-schwarzburg-arnstadt"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gunther-xli-of-schwarzburg-arnstadt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Günther XLI of Schwarzburg-Arnstadt</span><span class="tp">1529–1583</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ole-romer"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ole-romer.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ole Rømer</span><span class="tp">1644–1710</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-william-ii-of-prussia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-william-ii-of-prussia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Frederick William II of Prussia</span><span class="tp">1744–1797</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/fletcher-christian"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/fletcher-christian.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Fletcher Christian</span><span class="tp">1764–1793</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/armand-emmanuel-du-plessis-duc-de-richelieu"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/armand-emmanuel-du-plessis-duc-de-richelieu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Armand-Emmanuel du Plessis, Duc de Richelieu</span><span class="tp">1766–1822</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/billy-hughes"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/billy-hughes.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Billy Hughes</span><span class="tp">1862–1952</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/plutarco-elias-calles"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/plutarco-elias-calles.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Plutarco Elías Calles</span><span class="tp">1877–1945</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lu-xun"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lu-xun.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Lu Xun</span><span class="tp">1881–1936</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/eric-williams"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/eric-williams.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Eric Williams</span><span class="tp">1911–1981</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/robert-muldoon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/robert-muldoon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Robert Muldoon</span><span class="tp">1921–1992</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hammer-deroburt"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hammer-deroburt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hammer DeRoburt</span><span class="tp">1922–1992</span></span></a></li></ul><details class="cen-all"><summary>Show 2 more</summary><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/dmitri-shostakovich"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Dmitri Shostakovich</span><span class="tp">1906–1975</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/adolfo-suarez"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/adolfo-suarez.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Adolfo Suárez</span><span class="tp">1932–2014</span></span></a></li></ul></details></section>
